        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add Herdr plugin",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add a Herdr plugin manifest with boxes, warmup, prewarm, connect, repository job, and doctor actions\n- add a hidden Crabbox adapter that safely consumes Herdr invocation context without requiring jq, Python, or Node at runtime\n- add build/path pinning, documentation, packaging tests, and CLI unit tests\n\n## Why\n\nHerdr can install executable workflow plugins directly from GitHub subdirectories. This gives Crabbox users native Herdr actions and managed panes while keeping provider credentials, lease ownership, repository sync, and job behavior inside the Crabbox CLI.\n\n## User impact\n\nAfter a compatible Crabbox release, users can install the integration with:\n\n```sh\nherdr plugin install openclaw/crabbox/plugins/herdr\n```\n\nThe plugin does not install keybindings or lifecycle hooks. Normal Crabbox job stop policies still apply. Its install probe rejects older Crabbox binaries before registration.\n\n## Maintainer decision and publication\n\nCrabbox will sponsor this optional first-party integration. The provider-neutral core remains the authority for credentials, provisioning, repository sync, leases, and jobs; the Herdr-specific surface is a narrow hidden invocation adapter plus the plugin package and tests.\n\nThis PR lands the unreleased implementation only. It does not publish a Crabbox release or add the `herdr-plugin` repository topic. Add that topic only after a compatible Crabbox release ships, so marketplace discovery never advertises an unusable default-branch install.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `go test -race ./...`\n- `go build -trimpath -o /tmp/crabbox ./cmd/crabbox`\n- `go test -race ./internal/cli -run 'TestHerdrPlugin|TestNonBlankLines' -count=20`\n- `node --test scripts/herdr-plugin.test.js`\n- `scripts/check-docs.sh`\n- full branch AutoReview against `origin/main`: clean, no accepted/actionable findings; patch correct at 0.93 confidence\n- source-blind behavior contract: 6 pass, 0 fail, 0 blocked\n- Herdr 0.7.4 GitHub install resolved exact head `739a4330b69e7ca811825aa0ce82d83ed792dcba`, ran the build, and registered six actions plus six panes without warnings\n- live action proof: boxes opened a read-only overlay with non-empty real inventory; doctor opened a workspace-aware split and preserved its result; run-job and connect opened workspace-aware tabs and cancelled before provisioning or SSH\n- cleanup proof: result panes closed, plugin uninstalled, registration became empty, server stopped, and isolated session/config state was removed\n\nThe live run found and fixed one Herdr 0.7.4 contract bug before landing: overlay panes must target Herdr's active pane implicitly, so the plugin no longer passes the rejected `--target-pane` flag for overlay placement. The regression test now enforces that contract.\n",
